claim.claim-text:
an elongate catheter shaft (12; 112; 260) having a distal end region and a proximal end region;
a stent (16; 116; 250) having a proximal end region (20; 120; 254), a distal end region (18; 118; 252), and a length extending therebetween, the stent (16; 116; 250) disposed about the distal end region of the elongate catheter shaft (12; 112; 260);
a handle (202) including an actuation assembly; and
a delivery sheath (21; 121; 208; 300) having a proximal end region and distal end region, the proximal end region affixed to a portion of the actuation assembly,
wherein the delivery sheath is disposed over the elongate catheter shaft (12; 112; 260) and the stent (16; 116; 250), the delivery sheath comprising:
an outer sheath (22; 122; 240) having a proximal end region and a distal end region;
an inner sheath (26; 126; 244) slidably disposed within the outer sheath (22; 122; 240), the inner sheath (26; 126; 244) having a proximal end region and a distal end region; and
a lubricant (30; 130; 248; 310) disposed between the inner sheath (26; 126; 244) and the outer sheath (22; 122; 240);
wherein the outer sheath (22; 122; 240) is configured to be proximally retracted independently of the inner sheath (26; 126; 244) over a distal portion of the stent (16; 116; 250) and simultaneously with the inner sheath (26; 126; 244) over a proximal portion of the stent (16; 116; 250).
